1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,321
An army's strength at departure is only the starting point.

2
00:00:04,321 --> 00:00:09,187
Before battle, its supplies, troop numbers and route can all change.

3
00:00:09,187 --> 00:00:14,409
We need to see when it actually arrives, how many of the original troops

4
00:00:14,409 --> 00:00:19,558
remain, how much supply it carries, and what it actually paid along the

5
00:00:19,558 --> 00:00:19,848
way.

6
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,991
This time, we follow Robert in version 1.20.0.4.

7
00:00:23,991 --> 00:00:26,894
First, we read the army panel's current

8
00:00:26,894 --> 00:00:29,872
values, then track changes during a real

9
00:00:29,872 --> 00:00:30,319
march.

10
00:00:30,319 --> 00:00:33,733
The mechanics explain how the game calculates;

11
00:00:33,733 --> 00:00:37,295
live records show what actually happened in this

12
00:00:37,295 --> 00:00:37,592
run.

13
00:00:37,592 --> 00:00:41,592
Together, they explain the army's condition on arrival.

14
00:00:42,267 --> 00:00:47,028
For this episode, we switch to Robert of Apulia in version 1.20.0.4.

15
00:00:47,028 --> 00:00:50,942
A new normal campaign gives us one consistent character

16
00:00:50,942 --> 00:00:55,070
origin, and separate normal loads let us observe different

17
00:00:55,070 --> 00:00:55,640
actions.

18
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:58,510
Each scene will identify its run and day.

19
00:00:58,510 --> 00:01:01,307
We can compare separate loads, but will

20
00:01:01,307 --> 00:01:03,888
not edit them into one uninterrupted

21
00:01:03,888 --> 00:01:04,461
session.

22
00:01:04,461 --> 00:01:07,115
William's troop counts from the older

23
00:01:07,115 --> 00:01:09,984
version will not be overlaid on Robert's

24
00:01:09,984 --> 00:01:10,343
army.

25
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,397
First, keep three distinctions clear.

26
00:01:13,397 --> 00:01:17,414
Supply stock is material; actual troop strength counts people.

27
00:01:17,414 --> 00:01:22,662
A character record showing 1/1 does not automatically mean one soldier was added.

28
00:01:22,662 --> 00:01:26,224
Movement locking is another distinction: after Stop is

29
00:01:26,224 --> 00:01:29,785
pressed, the army may still have to finish its current

30
00:01:29,785 --> 00:01:30,048
leg.

31
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:33,928
These affect what we mean by 'recovered,' 'lost troops' and

32
00:01:33,928 --> 00:01:38,334
'stopped.' We will examine the actual records before explaining the

33
00:01:38,334 --> 00:01:38,860
changes.

34
00:01:39,533 --> 00:01:42,673
Troops can be lost through different processes.

35
00:01:42,673 --> 00:01:46,811
Periodic siege and raid processing, and movement attrition on

36
00:01:46,811 --> 00:01:51,152
entering a new county, have their own conditions and calculation

37
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:51,559
order.

38
00:01:51,559 --> 00:01:53,496
Not every loss is starvation.

39
00:01:53,496 --> 00:01:58,640
Replenishment, splitting, merging and other events can also change the total.

40
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:02,348
To explain a march, first compare each regiment's exact

41
00:02:02,348 --> 00:02:06,190
counts, then identify which processing actually occurred.

42
00:02:06,190 --> 00:02:10,465
A net change between readings is reported as a net change first.

43
00:02:11,133 --> 00:02:13,579
A march has several kinds of timing.

44
00:02:13,579 --> 00:02:17,788
The map preview gives a plan; the army window gives a current

45
00:02:17,788 --> 00:02:21,791
estimate; the first leg has its own progress and remaining

46
00:02:21,791 --> 00:02:22,412
duration.

47
00:02:22,412 --> 00:02:24,722
Actual arrival is a later outcome.

48
00:02:24,722 --> 00:02:29,749
Different figures for the whole route and its first leg need not conflict.

49
00:02:29,749 --> 00:02:34,023
We will label their scope, then verify arrival from the actual

50
00:02:34,023 --> 00:02:38,847
position and remaining route, rather than making one date mean several

51
00:02:38,847 --> 00:02:39,329
things.

52
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,107
Marching as one army aims to reduce arrangements along the way.

53
00:02:44,107 --> 00:02:48,344
Splitting to rest takes time at separate stations and to regroup.

54
00:02:48,344 --> 00:02:52,451
Rerouting requires completing the chosen sequence of waypoints.

55
00:02:52,451 --> 00:02:55,318
To compare these plans, start from the same

56
00:02:55,318 --> 00:02:57,518
normal save and head for the same

57
00:02:57,518 --> 00:02:58,318
destination.

58
00:02:58,318 --> 00:03:01,116
Record each plan's actual arrival outcome,

59
00:03:01,116 --> 00:03:04,114
then compare where the armies are on the same

60
00:03:04,114 --> 00:03:04,380
day.

61
00:03:05,033 --> 00:03:08,822
Before departure, establish what the army currently has.

62
00:03:08,822 --> 00:03:13,694
During the march, check which conditions change with location and route.

63
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:17,483
Before battle, confirm how many troops actually arrived.

64
00:03:17,483 --> 00:03:21,403
We begin with supply: separate what the army carries, how

65
00:03:21,403 --> 00:03:25,187
much it can carry, and how many troops the location can

66
00:03:25,187 --> 00:03:25,737
support.

67
00:03:25,737 --> 00:03:29,221
Then we can discuss where to stop, when to move on,

68
00:03:29,221 --> 00:03:32,773
and whether splitting really reduces local pressure.

69
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:39,757
Read the army's current and maximum strength, then expand each regiment.

70
00:03:39,757 --> 00:03:42,455
Locate deficits by comparing current

71
00:03:42,455 --> 00:03:44,778
and maximum values for the same

72
00:03:44,778 --> 00:03:45,453
regiment.

73
00:03:45,453 --> 00:03:50,929
To explain actual replenishment, also check the underlying soldier records.

74
00:03:50,929 --> 00:03:55,529
Keep confirmed character records with no soldier DATA separate.

75
00:03:55,529 --> 00:03:59,435
This avoids combining counts from different armies or

76
00:03:59,435 --> 00:04:03,488
treating a character's 1/1 display as an added soldier.

77
00:04:04,167 --> 00:04:08,535
Carried supply and supply capacity use the same supply unit.

78
00:04:08,535 --> 00:04:11,947
For a hypothetical example, 100 supply and 300

79
00:04:11,947 --> 00:04:15,582
capacity means the army carries 100 units and can

80
00:04:15,582 --> 00:04:16,324
carry 300.

81
00:04:16,324 --> 00:04:20,473
The first number is neither 100 soldiers nor 100 percent.

82
00:04:20,473 --> 00:04:25,642
The local supply limit must instead be compared with local troop usage.

83
00:04:25,642 --> 00:04:30,083
Get the units right before choosing which columns to compare.

84
00:04:30,733 --> 00:04:34,178
Carried supply, carrying capacity and the number of

85
00:04:34,178 --> 00:04:37,758
soldiers a location can support have their own units.

86
00:04:37,758 --> 00:04:40,430
If both armies remain in the same place

87
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:42,966
after a split, check the actual local

88
00:04:42,966 --> 00:04:43,377
usage.

89
00:04:43,377 --> 00:04:46,185
Looking only at the smaller army does not

90
00:04:46,185 --> 00:04:48,308
establish that the pressure has

91
00:04:48,308 --> 00:04:49,130
disappeared.

92
00:04:49,130 --> 00:04:52,809
After moving, read the new location's conditions again.

93
00:04:53,467 --> 00:04:56,051
The sign of the monthly supply change

94
00:04:56,051 --> 00:04:58,357
shows its direction under current

95
00:04:58,357 --> 00:04:59,125
conditions.

96
00:04:59,125 --> 00:05:03,148
It can change with location, usage or commander conditions.

97
00:05:03,148 --> 00:05:06,960
When an update is allowed, the game adds the applicable

98
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:10,841
change to stock, then clamps it between zero and current

99
00:05:10,841 --> 00:05:11,465
capacity.

100
00:05:11,465 --> 00:05:15,003
Reading the monthly figure does not itself apply an

101
00:05:15,003 --> 00:05:18,681
update, and it is not automatically divided by thirty

102
00:05:18,681 --> 00:05:19,305
each day.

103
00:05:19,305 --> 00:05:23,055
Read the actual stock again to see how much was gained.

104
00:05:23,733 --> 00:05:27,181
Supply recovery concerns the material carried by the

105
00:05:27,181 --> 00:05:30,629
army; troop recovery concerns actual soldiers in its

106
00:05:30,629 --> 00:05:31,292
regiments.

107
00:05:31,292 --> 00:05:33,443
The game handles them separately.

108
00:05:33,443 --> 00:05:37,345
More supply does not automatically fill troop deficits, and

109
00:05:37,345 --> 00:05:41,842
replenishment eligibility cannot be determined just by whether stock

110
00:05:41,842 --> 00:05:42,371
is full.

111
00:05:42,371 --> 00:05:47,225
Before marching on, read the stock, expand the actual regiments, and check

112
00:05:47,225 --> 00:05:52,145
current strength, maximum strength and replenishment conditions separately.

113
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:56,037
The selected small army has four actual soldier

114
00:05:56,037 --> 00:05:59,274
records totaling 250 men, all at full strength.

115
00:05:59,274 --> 00:06:03,288
In the paused query, all four currently have replenishment

116
00:06:03,288 --> 00:06:07,718
permission set to false, and their stored prepared fractions are

117
00:06:07,718 --> 00:06:08,065
zero.

118
00:06:08,065 --> 00:06:11,670
In the source code, a type flag shared by these four

119
00:06:11,670 --> 00:06:15,552
blocks current permission before the toggle and resource

120
00:06:15,552 --> 00:06:16,038
checks.

121
00:06:16,038 --> 00:06:20,296
This establishes these records' present eligibility; the label

122
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:24,692
'special troops' alone cannot describe armies from every source.

123
00:06:25,367 --> 00:06:28,206
Replenishment also has an order of operations.

124
00:06:28,206 --> 00:06:31,723
The normal preparation phase saves this round's prepared

125
00:06:31,723 --> 00:06:35,114
fraction according to conditions in the fixed physical

126
00:06:35,114 --> 00:06:35,428
slot.

127
00:06:35,428 --> 00:06:40,737
Some types first check current permission; some definition branches bypass that check.

128
00:06:40,737 --> 00:06:45,026
When calculating the actual replenishment request, the game reads the

129
00:06:45,026 --> 00:06:49,378
stored fraction, then checks current conditions in each physical slot.

130
00:06:49,378 --> 00:06:52,770
The currently calculated fraction, the stored fraction

131
00:06:52,770 --> 00:06:55,848
and the final number added must therefore be read

132
00:06:55,848 --> 00:06:56,539
separately.

133
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:01,008
Because of this timing, current permission being false does

134
00:07:01,008 --> 00:07:04,815
not automatically erase a positive fraction stored earlier.

135
00:07:04,815 --> 00:07:09,582
The request phase reads that older fraction and checks the physical slots'

136
00:07:09,582 --> 00:07:14,414
current conditions; it does not rerun that whole-regiment permission check.

137
00:07:14,414 --> 00:07:17,389
Conversely, a positive fraction calculated now

138
00:07:17,389 --> 00:07:20,429
does not guarantee soldiers will be added next.

139
00:07:20,429 --> 00:07:24,781
The request may be refused, or the integer result may still be zero.

140
00:07:24,781 --> 00:07:28,876
Verify replenishment through the actual soldier-count writeback.

141
00:07:29,533 --> 00:07:34,862
The military page's monthly replenishment toggle must also be tied to the troops' source.

142
00:07:34,862 --> 00:07:38,872
In troop-definition branches requiring this check, the game traces

143
00:07:38,872 --> 00:07:42,336
the soldiers to their actual source character, reads that

144
00:07:42,336 --> 00:07:46,225
character's military replenishment toggle, then checks resources

145
00:07:46,225 --> 00:07:47,015
and location.

146
00:07:47,015 --> 00:07:51,685
If the source is a vassal, the player's own checkbox cannot substitute for it.

147
00:07:51,685 --> 00:07:54,858
Other definition branches do not use the same toggle.

148
00:07:54,858 --> 00:07:58,689
Before acting, establish who supplied the troops being observed.

149
00:07:59,367 --> 00:08:02,302
When choosing a rest location, first read its

150
00:08:02,302 --> 00:08:05,693
monthly supply change, then wait for an actual stock

151
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:06,149
update.

152
00:08:06,149 --> 00:08:10,405
A positive monthly value is a reading under current conditions; an

153
00:08:10,405 --> 00:08:14,660
actual increase in stock proves that supplies recovered this time.

154
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:17,028
Replenishment needs a separate check.

155
00:08:17,028 --> 00:08:19,713
Full supply or a refreshed prepared value

156
00:08:19,713 --> 00:08:22,202
does not itself mean any soldiers were

157
00:08:22,202 --> 00:08:22,595
added.

158
00:08:23,267 --> 00:08:26,115
Splitting and merging handle supply differently.

159
00:08:26,115 --> 00:08:31,219
A newly split army first copies the source's stock; it does not halve it by headcount.

160
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:35,670
Each army's capacity still depends on its current commander and conditions.

161
00:08:35,670 --> 00:08:41,130
Merging first saves both original stocks and their weights for their respective merge roles.

162
00:08:41,130 --> 00:08:46,234
After selecting the commander and adjusting composition, it reads the merged capacity.

163
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:49,013
The 250 actual soldiers were conserved in this

164
00:08:49,013 --> 00:08:52,397
small-army case, but supply need not be conserved in the

165
00:08:52,397 --> 00:08:52,941
same way.

166
00:08:52,941 --> 00:08:56,383
Read back merged stock, capacity and commander separately.

167
00:08:57,033 --> 00:09:00,446
In the verified normal path with positive weights, merging

168
00:09:00,446 --> 00:09:03,977
calculates each army's weight share and truncates each to an

169
00:09:03,977 --> 00:09:04,448
integer.

170
00:09:04,448 --> 00:09:07,107
Each share is then multiplied by its original

171
00:09:07,107 --> 00:09:10,002
stock and truncated again, before the results are

172
00:09:10,002 --> 00:09:10,357
added.

173
00:09:10,357 --> 00:09:15,744
The shares may total slightly less than 100 percent; the game does not restore the remainder.

174
00:09:15,744 --> 00:09:18,808
The total stock is then clamped between zero and the

175
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:22,108
actual merged capacity, so this is not a single ordinary

176
00:09:22,108 --> 00:09:22,579
average.

177
00:09:22,579 --> 00:09:27,503
Large values have a separate safeguard branch and cannot use this simplified formula.

178
00:09:27,503 --> 00:09:30,341
Check the final stock against the actual reading.

179
00:09:32,067 --> 00:09:34,876
To explain falling troop numbers, separate

180
00:09:34,876 --> 00:09:38,019
current tooltips from changes that have already

181
00:09:38,019 --> 00:09:38,621
happened.

182
00:09:38,621 --> 00:09:42,717
The current attrition rate shows how conditions are calculated

183
00:09:42,717 --> 00:09:46,945
now; an integer budget sets the planned allocation for one pass.

184
00:09:46,945 --> 00:09:50,414
Actual losses require before-and-after writes to the

185
00:09:50,414 --> 00:09:54,017
physical soldier count, checked against replenishment,

186
00:09:54,017 --> 00:09:57,752
combat, splitting, merging, and other events in the same

187
00:09:57,752 --> 00:09:58,219
window.

188
00:09:58,219 --> 00:10:00,904
This avoids counting a budget twice as a

189
00:10:00,904 --> 00:10:03,388
loss, or calling every net decrease a

190
00:10:03,388 --> 00:10:03,791
death.

191
00:10:04,467 --> 00:10:07,219
First, how does the game prepare losses?

192
00:10:07,219 --> 00:10:10,384
Supply, siege, and raiding each have a budget.

193
00:10:10,384 --> 00:10:13,309
Siege and raiding are converted separately

194
00:10:13,309 --> 00:10:16,233
to integers, then combined for allocation.

195
00:10:16,233 --> 00:10:20,222
These budgets are set before the first soldier write, but

196
00:10:20,222 --> 00:10:23,862
later allocations use troop counts that have already

197
00:10:23,862 --> 00:10:24,422
changed.

198
00:10:24,422 --> 00:10:27,856
Adding the displayed rates and multiplying by one

199
00:10:27,856 --> 00:10:31,570
total misses the intermediate rounding and processing

200
00:10:31,570 --> 00:10:31,991
order.

201
00:10:32,667 --> 00:10:35,764
Siege and raiding share a combined stage.

202
00:10:35,764 --> 00:10:39,987
To attribute one specific deduction to siege, the siege

203
00:10:39,987 --> 00:10:44,595
budget actually used must be positive and the raiding budget

204
00:10:44,595 --> 00:10:44,979
zero.

205
00:10:44,979 --> 00:10:48,982
Then check the change in that physical soldier count.

206
00:10:48,982 --> 00:10:51,923
The budget describes the planned loss;

207
00:10:51,923 --> 00:10:54,555
the soldier write shows the actual

208
00:10:54,555 --> 00:10:55,251
decrease.

209
00:10:55,251 --> 00:10:59,255
That one result does not represent the whole journey.

210
00:10:59,933 --> 00:11:03,606
Take a hypothetical example: 199 eligible

211
00:11:03,606 --> 00:11:07,547
soldiers at a 5% supply rate give an integer

212
00:11:07,547 --> 00:11:08,622
budget of 9.

213
00:11:08,622 --> 00:11:10,729
A 1% siege rate gives 1.

214
00:11:10,729 --> 00:11:13,976
Calculated separately, they total 10.

215
00:11:13,976 --> 00:11:18,365
Combine the rates into 6% first, and 199 gives 11.

216
00:11:18,365 --> 00:11:21,173
This illustrates rounding order.

217
00:11:21,173 --> 00:11:24,768
Allocation to individual regiments still

218
00:11:24,768 --> 00:11:28,094
depends on their troop counts at that

219
00:11:28,094 --> 00:11:28,633
stage.

220
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:34,427
On this county-entry path, the game first calculates the army-wide budget

221
00:11:34,427 --> 00:11:38,992
and the total the preferred regiments can absorb, then stores the

222
00:11:38,992 --> 00:11:39,765
difference.

223
00:11:39,765 --> 00:11:42,319
If those regiments already cover the

224
00:11:42,319 --> 00:11:45,228
budget, county remainder allocation never

225
00:11:45,228 --> 00:11:45,724
starts.

226
00:11:45,724 --> 00:11:50,229
The second part runs only when the stored difference is positive.

227
00:11:50,229 --> 00:11:55,288
So county attrition does not always produce a remainder stage to inspect.

228
00:11:55,967 --> 00:12:00,972
That difference is fixed before deductions from the preferred regiments.

229
00:12:00,972 --> 00:12:06,185
Later allocation consumes the integer amounts requested from each regiment.

230
00:12:06,185 --> 00:12:11,397
If a write is skipped, or the actual change differs from the request, that

231
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:16,467
amount is not automatically refunded to recalculate the county remainder

232
00:12:16,467 --> 00:12:16,960
budget.

233
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:19,594
Keep the budget, requests, and actual

234
00:12:19,594 --> 00:12:22,512
physical decrease separate: they need not

235
00:12:22,512 --> 00:12:22,939
match.

236
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:27,236
County attrition modifiers also work in stages.

237
00:12:27,236 --> 00:12:30,755
Consider hypothetical inputs: 3,001 soldiers,

238
00:12:30,755 --> 00:12:34,430
a base rate of 5%, and a multiplier of 0.33339.

239
00:12:34,430 --> 00:12:37,672
The effective rate is first calculated as

240
00:12:37,672 --> 00:12:40,834
1.666%, then applied to the troop count,

241
00:12:40,834 --> 00:12:41,625
giving 49.

242
00:12:41,625 --> 00:12:46,730
The corresponding modified minimum is 33, so this example uses 49.

243
00:12:46,730 --> 00:12:49,276
Applying everything together and

244
00:12:49,276 --> 00:12:52,061
rounding only at the end would give

245
00:12:52,061 --> 00:12:52,300
50.

246
00:12:52,967 --> 00:12:55,628
Location checks also have a defined scope.

247
00:12:55,628 --> 00:12:59,589
The next-step replenishment location check uses the first stop

248
00:12:59,589 --> 00:13:03,550
in the army's stored route, not its distant final destination.

249
00:13:03,550 --> 00:13:08,110
The game checks that province and the native condition between the army

250
00:13:08,110 --> 00:13:12,670
owner and the local holder; this is more specific than general military

251
00:13:12,670 --> 00:13:13,120
access.

252
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:16,288
Without a complete route, keep the result unknown.

253
00:13:16,288 --> 00:13:21,549
In the conditional projection, a passing check substitutes only the location input.

254
00:13:21,549 --> 00:13:25,795
Preparation ratios and other conditions still need separate checks.

255
00:13:26,467 --> 00:13:30,197
Once the army-wide budget is an integer, it is allocated to

256
00:13:30,197 --> 00:13:33,927
regiments in order, then written to physical soldier slots.

257
00:13:33,927 --> 00:13:37,250
Each step has its own denominator, cap, and rounding.

258
00:13:37,250 --> 00:13:41,827
A regiment's requested amount need not equal the final physical decrease.

259
00:13:41,827 --> 00:13:44,772
Within that individual write, count a physical

260
00:13:44,772 --> 00:13:47,588
slot referenced by several data entries only

261
00:13:47,588 --> 00:13:47,908
once.

262
00:13:47,908 --> 00:13:53,175
Fractions discarded here are not retained as fractional soldiers in this write path.

263
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:56,950
Supply can read zero both before and after

264
00:13:56,950 --> 00:14:00,141
an update without the update being skipped.

265
00:14:00,141 --> 00:14:04,682
In the source's successful path, the change is still added, a

266
00:14:04,682 --> 00:14:09,447
negative result is clamped to zero, and supply-loss calculations

267
00:14:09,447 --> 00:14:10,117
continue.

268
00:14:10,117 --> 00:14:14,224
So zero-to-zero stock can accompany a successful update.

269
00:14:14,224 --> 00:14:16,485
Whether soldiers were deducted

270
00:14:16,485 --> 00:14:19,198
requires the later budget and actual

271
00:14:19,198 --> 00:14:19,725
writes.

272
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:25,320
Zero stock does not add another tier in this ordinary supply chain.

273
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:30,165
Suppose the loaded vanilla thresholds are 60, 10, and 0: zero and

274
00:14:30,165 --> 00:14:34,861
9.99999 fall in the same tier, while exactly 10 enters the tier

275
00:14:34,861 --> 00:14:35,308
above.

276
00:14:35,308 --> 00:14:38,534
Commander modifiers, fleet suppression, and

277
00:14:38,534 --> 00:14:41,759
eligible troop counts also affect the final

278
00:14:41,759 --> 00:14:42,285
budget.

279
00:14:42,285 --> 00:14:45,332
Zero stock is neither proof of safety nor

280
00:14:45,332 --> 00:14:48,380
a fixed 5% deduction from every regiment.

281
00:14:49,033 --> 00:14:52,164
Small armies also meet whole-soldier rounding.

282
00:14:52,164 --> 00:14:55,698
At a hypothetical effective rate of 5%, 19 eligible

283
00:14:55,698 --> 00:14:59,578
soldiers produce an army-wide budget of zero; 20 produce

284
00:14:59,578 --> 00:14:59,855
one.

285
00:14:59,855 --> 00:15:03,870
This step has no minimum deduction of one soldier per pass.

286
00:15:03,870 --> 00:15:06,661
But that explains only the supply budget.

287
00:15:06,661 --> 00:15:11,153
Siege, county entry, and other troop changes need separate checks.

288
00:15:11,153 --> 00:15:16,461
A missing event in the log does not prove zero losses across the whole window.

289
00:15:18,167 --> 00:15:22,535
For a route, distinguish three timings: the expected arrival

290
00:15:22,535 --> 00:15:27,048
before ordering, the current estimate while moving, and actual

291
00:15:27,048 --> 00:15:27,630
arrival.

292
00:15:27,630 --> 00:15:30,206
A preview describes the plan; after

293
00:15:30,206 --> 00:15:32,708
the order, read the route actually

294
00:15:32,708 --> 00:15:33,223
stored.

295
00:15:33,223 --> 00:15:38,672
At the observation endpoint, check the current location and remaining route.

296
00:15:38,672 --> 00:15:43,619
In this reroute test, later independent state confirmed the endpoint.

297
00:15:43,619 --> 00:15:47,347
A preview line reaching it was not proof of arrival.

298
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,536
The army window's full-route arrival estimate and

299
00:15:51,536 --> 00:15:54,856
the time left on the first leg cover different

300
00:15:54,856 --> 00:15:55,361
scopes.

301
00:15:55,361 --> 00:15:59,431
Land and sea movement speeds have their own readings too;

302
00:15:59,431 --> 00:16:03,643
neither is directly the remaining days for the whole route.

303
00:16:03,643 --> 00:16:08,597
Label comparisons as speed, first-leg duration, or final arrival date.

304
00:16:08,597 --> 00:16:12,409
Without complete readings from the same paused frame,

305
00:16:12,409 --> 00:16:16,869
subtracting old dates would invent a precise-looking later-leg

306
00:16:16,869 --> 00:16:17,516
duration.

307
00:16:18,167 --> 00:16:21,600
Actual duration also needs a clear starting point.

308
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:25,754
In this reroute test, 13 calendar days passed from the march

309
00:16:25,754 --> 00:16:29,909
start after an independent load to the alternative endpoint.

310
00:16:29,909 --> 00:16:35,059
From the replacement route order to that endpoint, it took 8 calendar days.

311
00:16:35,059 --> 00:16:38,836
Both are observed outcomes with different time origins.

312
00:16:38,836 --> 00:16:41,647
They are not interchangeable, and cannot

313
00:16:41,647 --> 00:16:44,318
rank direct march, split-and-rest, and

314
00:16:44,318 --> 00:16:44,810
detour.

315
00:16:44,810 --> 00:16:49,411
Each strategy still needs to finish from the common starting point.

316
00:16:50,067 --> 00:16:52,998
Immediately before and after the reroute,

317
00:16:52,998 --> 00:16:55,572
the game date and army location were

318
00:16:55,572 --> 00:16:56,287
unchanged.

319
00:16:56,287 --> 00:16:59,782
What changed was the stored route's later section.

320
00:16:59,782 --> 00:17:03,976
Accepting the order did not move the army to a new location.

321
00:17:03,976 --> 00:17:07,575
Advancing game time later showed it at the original

322
00:17:07,575 --> 00:17:11,315
first-leg endpoint and then the alternative endpoint.

323
00:17:11,315 --> 00:17:14,869
Keep the same-day order result separate from later

324
00:17:14,869 --> 00:17:18,565
movement, so an acknowledgment is not presented as a

325
00:17:18,565 --> 00:17:19,703
completed march.

326
00:17:20,367 --> 00:17:22,467
Now consider movement lock.

327
00:17:22,467 --> 00:17:25,962
Before the stop test, first-leg progress was

328
00:17:25,962 --> 00:17:29,774
about 96.7%, and the threshold actually read was

329
00:17:29,774 --> 00:17:30,092
50%.

330
00:17:30,092 --> 00:17:34,214
This percentage describes the current first leg, not

331
00:17:34,214 --> 00:17:37,860
over 90% of the whole journey: three more legs

332
00:17:37,860 --> 00:17:38,573
remained.

333
00:17:38,573 --> 00:17:41,674
To know the choices left after locking,

334
00:17:41,674 --> 00:17:45,013
inspect the actual route after stopping or

335
00:17:45,013 --> 00:17:45,809
rerouting.

336
00:17:45,809 --> 00:17:50,555
One percentage alone cannot tell us where the army will stop.

337
00:17:51,233 --> 00:17:54,116
Both lock tests used progress strictly

338
00:17:54,116 --> 00:17:57,074
above the threshold read for that test.

339
00:17:57,074 --> 00:17:59,151
They show what stopping and

340
00:17:59,151 --> 00:18:01,691
rerouting actually retained after

341
00:18:01,691 --> 00:18:02,614
crossing it.

342
00:18:02,614 --> 00:18:07,179
The current route code selects a committed first leg using a

343
00:18:07,179 --> 00:18:11,668
strict greater-than comparison; equality falls on the other

344
00:18:11,668 --> 00:18:12,049
side.

345
00:18:12,049 --> 00:18:13,696
That is the code rule.

346
00:18:13,696 --> 00:18:17,658
Neither test measured stopping or rerouting at exact

347
00:18:17,658 --> 00:18:21,696
equality, so these results do not verify the equality

348
00:18:21,696 --> 00:18:22,381
boundary.

349
00:18:23,033 --> 00:18:26,008
After locking, we issued stop just once.

350
00:18:26,008 --> 00:18:30,394
A later independent read showed the four-leg route reduced

351
00:18:30,394 --> 00:18:34,251
to its original first stop, with first-leg progress

352
00:18:34,251 --> 00:18:35,007
preserved.

353
00:18:35,007 --> 00:18:37,312
The army did not stop in place.

354
00:18:37,312 --> 00:18:41,102
Two days later, it reached that first-leg endpoint

355
00:18:41,102 --> 00:18:44,967
with an empty route, and stayed there the following

356
00:18:44,967 --> 00:18:45,270
day.

357
00:18:45,270 --> 00:18:49,806
Stop removed later travel while completing the committed leg.

358
00:18:49,806 --> 00:18:52,473
The target field was not read then;

359
00:18:52,473 --> 00:18:55,520
actual location and route establish this

360
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:56,053
result.

361
00:18:56,733 --> 00:18:59,564
Rerouting was a separate normal march test.

362
00:18:59,564 --> 00:19:04,698
Three stops remained on the original route when we chose a different endpoint.

363
00:19:04,698 --> 00:19:09,174
After the new order, location and first-leg progress were unchanged.

364
00:19:09,174 --> 00:19:12,067
The original first stop remained, while the

365
00:19:12,067 --> 00:19:14,690
later route became a leg toward the new

366
00:19:14,690 --> 00:19:15,296
endpoint.

367
00:19:15,296 --> 00:19:19,014
We then observed the army reach the original first stop,

368
00:19:19,014 --> 00:19:22,866
followed by the alternative endpoint, with an empty route.

369
00:19:22,866 --> 00:19:27,473
Locking constrained the current leg without fixing every later choice.

370
00:19:28,133 --> 00:19:31,971
A route warning about paying an embarkation fee appears

371
00:19:31,971 --> 00:19:35,878
before ordering; actual payment needs separate evidence.

372
00:19:35,878 --> 00:19:40,716
After this army entered a sea zone, an independent cash query and the

373
00:19:40,716 --> 00:19:45,063
native payment chain matched a 3-gold debit for this account's

374
00:19:45,063 --> 00:19:45,904
embarkation.

375
00:19:45,904 --> 00:19:48,877
That is not a universal fee for every army.

376
00:19:48,877 --> 00:19:52,884
County-loss budgets are conditional too: they do not mean

377
00:19:52,884 --> 00:19:56,681
every province crossing must remove the same number of

378
00:19:56,681 --> 00:19:57,313
soldiers.

379
00:19:57,967 --> 00:20:02,938
When Robert's army entered the sea zone, its actual state became embarked.

380
00:20:02,938 --> 00:20:06,898
The native payment record identifies a 3-gold debit to the

381
00:20:06,898 --> 00:20:10,926
personal account, and the account balance fell by exactly 3

382
00:20:10,926 --> 00:20:11,267
gold.

383
00:20:11,267 --> 00:20:14,626
This establishes the payment for this embarkation.

384
00:20:14,626 --> 00:20:17,614
Other armies and routes still need their own

385
00:20:17,614 --> 00:20:20,739
fee checked; 3 gold is not a universal charge.

386
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:24,430
Route warnings help with choices before departure.

387
00:20:24,430 --> 00:20:27,270
Explaining later troop decreases also requires

388
00:20:27,270 --> 00:20:30,235
separating county-entry deductions from periodic

389
00:20:30,235 --> 00:20:30,852
attrition.

390
00:20:30,852 --> 00:20:33,609
In the source, they have distinct direct call

391
00:20:33,609 --> 00:20:36,487
entries and a shared remainder-allocation path.

392
00:20:36,487 --> 00:20:40,668
If the only record is from that shared path, the cause stays unknown.

393
00:20:40,668 --> 00:20:43,326
Crossing a county boundary does not justify

394
00:20:43,326 --> 00:20:46,170
attributing the whole decrease to county-entry

395
00:20:46,170 --> 00:20:46,788
attrition.

396
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:53,890
To compare the three plans, first ask four questions: how long until arrival, how many troops

397
00:20:53,890 --> 00:20:59,106
remain in the original regiments, how much supply each army has, and how much was actually

398
00:20:59,106 --> 00:20:59,395
paid.

399
00:20:59,395 --> 00:21:03,811
The state on arrival tells us what condition the route delivered the army in.

400
00:21:03,811 --> 00:21:06,558
The state on the same day tells us how far each

401
00:21:06,558 --> 00:21:09,540
arrangement has progressed after the same amount of

402
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:09,832
time.

403
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:15,369
Each of the three replays must reload the same normal starting save and

404
00:21:15,369 --> 00:21:20,033
check the character, date, commander, original regiments, stock, and

405
00:21:20,033 --> 00:21:20,650
treasury.

406
00:21:20,650 --> 00:21:23,422
Newly split armies are identified by the

407
00:21:23,422 --> 00:21:26,125
identities that actually appear in that

408
00:21:26,125 --> 00:21:26,402
run.

409
00:21:26,402 --> 00:21:29,887
This keeps any later extra entry, commander change,

410
00:21:29,887 --> 00:21:33,440
or missing original regiment visible in the results.

411
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:39,434
Plan A keeps the army intact and follows the direct route shown in this run's actual preview.

412
00:21:39,434 --> 00:21:42,272
After the order, first confirm that the route has

413
00:21:42,272 --> 00:21:45,111
taken effect, then track its position day by day.

414
00:21:45,111 --> 00:21:48,351
Actual arrival requires the army to be at the target, in

415
00:21:48,351 --> 00:21:51,649
an appropriate state, with the remaining route completed.

416
00:21:51,649 --> 00:21:56,008
Neither an estimated date nor an order confirmation can replace that moment.

417
00:21:56,667 --> 00:22:01,298
Plan B first splits the army, rests at two verified locations, then regroups.

418
00:22:01,298 --> 00:22:05,689
Each army's rest period starts on the day it actually becomes stationary.

419
00:22:05,689 --> 00:22:09,568
Once the preset stock and troop-shortfall conditions are met, or

420
00:22:09,568 --> 00:22:13,568
the preset stay expires, it leaves according to the original plan.

421
00:22:13,568 --> 00:22:16,394
Insufficient recovery is also a result of this

422
00:22:16,394 --> 00:22:18,851
plan; we cannot restart to obtain better

423
00:22:18,851 --> 00:22:19,343
numbers.

424
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:23,064
Plan C keeps the army intact, passes through the legal

425
00:22:23,064 --> 00:22:25,958
waypoints chosen in advance, then heads to the same

426
00:22:25,958 --> 00:22:26,639
destination.

427
00:22:26,639 --> 00:22:29,142
It changes the route, while supply and troop

428
00:22:29,142 --> 00:22:31,874
counts are recorded as they actually stand along

429
00:22:31,874 --> 00:22:32,329
the way.

430
00:22:32,329 --> 00:22:36,290
Each leg waits for actual arrival before turning toward the next point.

431
00:22:36,290 --> 00:22:39,916
Moving the camera there cannot stand in for the army reaching it.

432
00:22:40,567 --> 00:22:44,387
The balanced-split code first creates a new army, then transfers

433
00:22:44,387 --> 00:22:48,087
whole army-regiment records according to weights for different

434
00:22:48,087 --> 00:22:48,744
categories.

435
00:22:48,744 --> 00:22:52,832
This normal path does not cut every persistent troop slot in half, so

436
00:22:52,832 --> 00:22:56,979
the two displayed troop counts are not guaranteed to be exactly equal.

437
00:22:56,979 --> 00:23:00,862
Creating the new army also copies the original supply-stock field.

438
00:23:00,862 --> 00:23:04,567
Whether that stock hits the new capacity limit must be checked

439
00:23:04,567 --> 00:23:08,092
through the separate supply update and the actual resulting

440
00:23:08,092 --> 00:23:08,451
state.

441
00:23:09,133 --> 00:23:12,126
Splitting a hundred troops into two groups of fifty

442
00:23:12,126 --> 00:23:15,118
does not make the same location support only fifty.

443
00:23:15,118 --> 00:23:19,127
Take a hypothetical case: aggregate local usage is six thousand, the

444
00:23:19,127 --> 00:23:22,899
limit is four thousand, and the selected army has only a hundred

445
00:23:22,899 --> 00:23:23,312
troops.

446
00:23:23,312 --> 00:23:27,026
If both armies remain in the same province and the contributing

447
00:23:27,026 --> 00:23:30,800
regiments and their eligibility are unchanged, usage remains six

448
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:31,330
thousand.

449
00:23:31,330 --> 00:23:34,175
Whether splitting improves supply depends on how

450
00:23:34,175 --> 00:23:36,961
actual usage changes and where each army really

451
00:23:36,961 --> 00:23:37,257
goes.

452
00:23:37,933 --> 00:23:42,247
After splitting, list each army's stock and capacity separately.

453
00:23:42,247 --> 00:23:45,074
Stock is what each army actually carries;

454
00:23:45,074 --> 00:23:47,833
capacity is what that army can currently

455
00:23:47,833 --> 00:23:48,246
carry.

456
00:23:48,246 --> 00:23:51,414
Keep each army's real values in the comparison.

457
00:23:51,414 --> 00:23:54,916
Adding the two stocks or taking an average does not

458
00:23:54,916 --> 00:23:58,349
produce the supply of an intact army that does not

459
00:23:58,349 --> 00:23:58,761
exist.

460
00:23:59,433 --> 00:24:04,235
After merging, check the commander again and expand the complete regiment list.

461
00:24:04,235 --> 00:24:07,027
An entry showing one current troop out of one

462
00:24:07,027 --> 00:24:09,942
maximum first tells us only that entry's actual

463
00:24:09,942 --> 00:24:10,314
count.

464
00:24:10,314 --> 00:24:12,745
It may have no ordinary troop-slot data.

465
00:24:12,745 --> 00:24:15,904
That number alone cannot identify it as a knight or

466
00:24:15,904 --> 00:24:18,629
show that one ordinary soldier has just been

467
00:24:18,629 --> 00:24:19,310
reinforced.

468
00:24:19,310 --> 00:24:23,261
Its specific category must be matched to its own native identity.

469
00:24:23,933 --> 00:24:26,758
Regrouping means both armies have reached the

470
00:24:26,758 --> 00:24:29,583
same place; only merging turns them into one.

471
00:24:29,583 --> 00:24:34,674
After the merge, reread stock, capacity, the actual commander, and every regiment.

472
00:24:34,674 --> 00:24:38,461
Count the original regiments separately from later additions.

473
00:24:38,461 --> 00:24:41,561
If a legal merge changes these conditions, retain

474
00:24:41,561 --> 00:24:44,344
those changes as actual consequences of this

475
00:24:44,344 --> 00:24:45,103
arrangement.

476
00:24:45,103 --> 00:24:47,990
Do not delete new entries or change commanders

477
00:24:47,990 --> 00:24:51,001
afterward to make the result match expectations.

478
00:24:51,667 --> 00:24:55,979
Separate current monthly figures from costs accumulated during the journey.

479
00:24:55,979 --> 00:25:00,521
Current monthly income minus full monthly expenditure gives current net income.

480
00:25:00,521 --> 00:25:03,446
These figures describe present income and spending

481
00:25:03,446 --> 00:25:06,780
conditions; they cannot be held constant across the whole

482
00:25:06,780 --> 00:25:07,248
journey.

483
00:25:07,248 --> 00:25:12,710
Reread them when the armies' raised status, troop sources, or other income and spending change.

484
00:25:12,710 --> 00:25:16,271
When comparing route costs, record cumulative actual payments

485
00:25:16,271 --> 00:25:20,064
separately, and retain income and other events over the same date

486
00:25:20,064 --> 00:25:20,415
range.

487
00:25:21,067 --> 00:25:24,887
The current monthly military-maintenance rate and the alternative

488
00:25:24,887 --> 00:25:28,589
monthly rate for the all-raised scenario describe two different

489
00:25:28,589 --> 00:25:29,236
situations.

490
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:31,669
They are not two expenses to add together.

491
00:25:31,669 --> 00:25:35,174
Full monthly expenditure already includes military costs, so

492
00:25:35,174 --> 00:25:38,795
using net income must not deduct the same military cost again.

493
00:25:38,795 --> 00:25:41,460
A monthly rate is still only the current rate.

494
00:25:41,460 --> 00:25:46,323
To state how much maintenance has actually been paid during the journey, the actual

495
00:25:46,323 --> 00:25:51,186
payment source, amount, and date must match; the treasury difference alone is not a

496
00:25:51,186 --> 00:25:51,831
substitute.

497
00:25:52,500 --> 00:25:54,295
Keep a separate cost ledger.

498
00:25:54,295 --> 00:25:58,655
Reconcile embarkation payments, military maintenance, income during

499
00:25:58,655 --> 00:26:02,754
the period, and other spending within the same account and date

500
00:26:02,754 --> 00:26:03,144
range.

501
00:26:03,144 --> 00:26:06,094
The treasury's net change mixes these sources.

502
00:26:06,094 --> 00:26:10,326
Even an increased balance can include military costs already paid.

503
00:26:10,326 --> 00:26:15,392
Military costs included in full expenditure must not be deducted a second time.

504
00:26:16,067 --> 00:26:20,541
The troop-strength table has two columns: one tracks only the regiments present

505
00:26:20,541 --> 00:26:24,845
at the start; the other retains all relevant armies actually held under that

506
00:26:24,845 --> 00:26:25,128
plan.

507
00:26:25,128 --> 00:26:30,274
One additional person cannot automatically cancel out a shortfall in the original regiments.

508
00:26:30,274 --> 00:26:34,749
Nor does a source army disappearing after a merge mean the entire army has died.

509
00:26:34,749 --> 00:26:40,231
Counts, identities, and organizational changes must be read together to see where the troops went.

510
00:26:40,900 --> 00:26:45,384
The arrival table first lists each plan's own arrival time and arrival state.

511
00:26:45,384 --> 00:26:48,293
The same-day table then lists the actual readings

512
00:26:48,293 --> 00:26:50,668
on days seven, fourteen, twenty-one, and

513
00:26:50,668 --> 00:26:51,440
twenty-eight.

514
00:26:51,440 --> 00:26:53,246
Read the two tables separately.

515
00:26:53,246 --> 00:26:56,011
Any additional recovery opportunities and costs

516
00:26:56,011 --> 00:26:58,894
from the longer journey are part of that journey.

517
00:26:58,894 --> 00:27:01,449
Troop counts from different dates cannot be

518
00:27:01,449 --> 00:27:04,182
presented directly as a same-day reinforcement

519
00:27:04,182 --> 00:27:04,776
advantage.

520
00:27:05,433 --> 00:27:09,292
The old replays did not establish a strict winner among the three plans.

521
00:27:09,292 --> 00:27:11,910
B stopped on day thirty-eight because the frozen

522
00:27:11,910 --> 00:27:14,855
conditions were not met, with fifty-two days of budget

523
00:27:14,855 --> 00:27:15,400
remaining.

524
00:27:15,400 --> 00:27:18,695
C retains fifteen two-day sampling deviations, so arrival can

525
00:27:18,695 --> 00:27:22,098
only be placed after day seventy-five and by day seventy-seven.

526
00:27:22,098 --> 00:27:23,813
These historical records remain.

527
00:27:23,813 --> 00:27:27,992
For the new comparison, we will discuss the trade-offs in actual routes, rest

528
00:27:27,992 --> 00:27:31,845
locations, and enemy conditions once all three independent replays have

529
00:27:31,845 --> 00:27:32,333
finished.

530
00:27:34,033 --> 00:27:37,019
Returning to troop-count changes, first distinguish the

531
00:27:37,019 --> 00:27:40,112
budget, actual troop deductions, and the whole army's net

532
00:27:40,112 --> 00:27:40,492
change.

533
00:27:40,492 --> 00:27:43,695
Siege and raid losses share a loss stage in the source code.

534
00:27:43,695 --> 00:27:47,459
Explaining a particular siege loss also requires checking that a siege

535
00:27:47,459 --> 00:27:51,222
was actually underway and that conditions such as no raiding were met.

536
00:27:51,222 --> 00:27:53,998
Allocation has its own order and integer remainders.

537
00:27:53,998 --> 00:27:56,853
Multiplying the displayed percentage by each regiment

538
00:27:56,853 --> 00:27:59,709
does not produce a ledger of actual troop deductions.

539
00:28:00,367 --> 00:28:04,354
Low supply also depends on the threshold table loaded for that run.

540
00:28:04,354 --> 00:28:08,099
At the vanilla boundary of ten, nine point nine nine nine nine

541
00:28:08,099 --> 00:28:12,026
nine is already below ten, while exactly ten remains on the other

542
00:28:12,026 --> 00:28:12,328
side.

543
00:28:12,328 --> 00:28:16,196
The game updates stock before calculating the supply-loss budget.

544
00:28:16,196 --> 00:28:19,827
Fleet, grace, and regiment conditions also affect the result.

545
00:28:19,827 --> 00:28:22,439
Low stock and how many troops were actually

546
00:28:22,439 --> 00:28:24,990
deducted must therefore still be confirmed

547
00:28:24,990 --> 00:28:25,659
separately.

548
00:28:26,333 --> 00:28:29,275
Before departure, review the first stop, final

549
00:28:29,275 --> 00:28:31,898
destination, and current arrival estimate

550
00:28:31,898 --> 00:28:32,473
together.

551
00:28:32,473 --> 00:28:36,546
A legal route only shows that this movement is currently allowed.

552
00:28:36,546 --> 00:28:39,360
Whether the army can rest along the way, and

553
00:28:39,360 --> 00:28:42,175
what it may pay, require their own condition

554
00:28:42,175 --> 00:28:42,623
checks.

555
00:28:42,623 --> 00:28:45,495
Save the current stock, troop shortfall, next

556
00:28:45,495 --> 00:28:48,942
location, and warnings to establish a baseline for the

557
00:28:48,942 --> 00:28:49,452
journey.

558
00:28:49,452 --> 00:28:52,804
After issuing the order, confirm the actual route; on

559
00:28:52,804 --> 00:28:56,281
actual arrival, compare reality with the original plan.

560
00:28:56,933 --> 00:29:00,873
Reread the current state when the monthly change turns from

561
00:29:00,873 --> 00:29:04,813
positive to negative, movement becomes locked, or the route

562
00:29:04,813 --> 00:29:05,347
changes.

563
00:29:05,347 --> 00:29:10,538
Unchanged stock can have several explanations: no permitted update opportunity

564
00:29:10,538 --> 00:29:15,463
yet, rejected conditions, a zero current contribution, or a gain capped by

565
00:29:15,463 --> 00:29:16,062
capacity.

566
00:29:16,062 --> 00:29:19,020
One unchanged number cannot distinguish them.

567
00:29:19,020 --> 00:29:22,826
Retain the dates, locations, stock, and update conditions

568
00:29:22,826 --> 00:29:27,033
before and after, then keep observing the changes that actually

569
00:29:27,033 --> 00:29:27,433
occur.

570
00:29:28,100 --> 00:29:33,145
After splitting or merging, check physical troop counts first, then characters and commanders.

571
00:29:33,145 --> 00:29:38,298
In this case, the selected small army split off a new army and merged it back into the original.

572
00:29:38,298 --> 00:29:42,216
Its four physical troop records continued to total two hundred and fifty.

573
00:29:42,216 --> 00:29:44,896
Meanwhile, a character record with no troop data,

574
00:29:44,896 --> 00:29:47,302
displayed as one out of one in another army,

575
00:29:47,302 --> 00:29:47,958
disappeared.

576
00:29:47,958 --> 00:29:53,057
The same character became commander of the new army, then of the original army after the merge.

577
00:29:53,057 --> 00:29:57,995
That one-out-of-one display change cannot be counted as one physical soldier gained or lost.

578
00:29:57,995 --> 00:30:03,040
Physical counts, character associations, and the current commander must be checked separately.

579
00:30:03,700 --> 00:30:06,495
After merging, a new entry showing one current troop

580
00:30:06,495 --> 00:30:09,397
and a maximum of one can also have a character source.

581
00:30:09,397 --> 00:30:13,869
A verified conditional branch creates a new army-regiment record while processing a

582
00:30:13,869 --> 00:30:18,233
former commander, associates it with that character, then refreshes the character

583
00:30:18,233 --> 00:30:18,556
cache.

584
00:30:18,556 --> 00:30:20,633
Its data list is empty at construction.

585
00:30:20,633 --> 00:30:25,638
A later one-out-of-one display does not directly mean an ordinary troop slot gained a soldier.

586
00:30:25,638 --> 00:30:29,520
Whether this is the new entry in this case, whether the character is the

587
00:30:29,520 --> 00:30:33,511
current commander, and whether the character is a knight must each be read

588
00:30:33,511 --> 00:30:34,104
separately.

589
00:30:34,767 --> 00:30:37,098
Read troop recovery in the same order.

590
00:30:37,098 --> 00:30:40,219
Reinforcement preparation values, eligibility, and

591
00:30:40,219 --> 00:30:43,465
calculated requests show how far the conditions have

592
00:30:43,465 --> 00:30:44,152
progressed.

593
00:30:44,152 --> 00:30:47,526
Actual additions require the writes to the troop slots.

594
00:30:47,526 --> 00:30:52,311
The net change across one update can also include zeroing and cache refreshes.

595
00:30:52,311 --> 00:30:54,443
After arrival, reread stock, troop

596
00:30:54,443 --> 00:30:57,077
shortfalls, and current conditions for the

597
00:30:57,077 --> 00:30:57,893
new location.

598
00:30:57,893 --> 00:31:02,003
Do not carry over old judgments from the sea or the starting point.

599
00:31:02,667 --> 00:31:07,378
Check payments once more: this example has a matched three-gold embarkation debit.

600
00:31:07,378 --> 00:31:10,415
The current monthly military-maintenance rate, total

601
00:31:10,415 --> 00:31:13,861
expenditure, and net treasury change can each help read the

602
00:31:13,861 --> 00:31:14,387
accounts.

603
00:31:14,387 --> 00:31:17,943
To state how much military maintenance was actually paid, the

604
00:31:17,943 --> 00:31:21,731
corresponding cost component still has to be linked to the actual

605
00:31:21,731 --> 00:31:22,373
settlement.

606
00:31:22,373 --> 00:31:26,567
Without that detail, leave the cost unknown; do not interpret it as free.

607
00:31:27,233 --> 00:31:29,928
This method can be taken to another machine.

608
00:31:29,928 --> 00:31:35,070
The reusable parts are the mechanics, reading methods, and order of checks: confirm

609
00:31:35,070 --> 00:31:40,213
the current game version, then align the character, army, date, and the same paused

610
00:31:40,213 --> 00:31:40,584
state.

611
00:31:40,584 --> 00:31:45,114
Which route was actually traveled, how many troops were lost, and whether

612
00:31:45,114 --> 00:31:49,519
payment really occurred must still be answered by the new session's own

613
00:31:49,519 --> 00:31:50,016
records.

614
00:31:50,016 --> 00:31:53,690
Retained originals allow old conclusions to be recalculated.

615
00:31:53,690 --> 00:31:57,181
They do not create a new march result on another machine.

616
00:31:57,833 --> 00:32:00,581
Before departure, read troop counts, stock, and route.

617
00:32:00,581 --> 00:32:02,668
During the journey, track actual changes.

618
00:32:02,668 --> 00:32:05,466
Before battle, confirm the army's actual arrival state.

619
00:32:05,466 --> 00:32:09,332
For Robert's stop after embarkation, issued while movement was unlocked, we

620
00:32:09,332 --> 00:32:13,249
verified that the route cleared and that the army remained in place the next

621
00:32:13,249 --> 00:32:13,456
day.

622
00:32:13,456 --> 00:32:15,745
That is the result of this particular action.

623
00:32:15,745 --> 00:32:20,426
Link each action to its own resulting state, then choose the next step using the conditions

624
00:32:20,426 --> 00:32:24,798
visible in this run, so the march plan keeps pace with the road the army has actually

625
00:32:24,798 --> 00:32:25,261
traveled.
